   "daf": "45b",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "נִמְצָא סָמוּךְ לַסְּפָר אוֹ לְעִיר שֶׁרוּבָּהּ נׇכְרִים כּוּ׳. דִּכְתִיב: ״כִּי יִמָּצֵא״ — פְּרָט לְמָצוּי.",
   "en": "§ The mishna taught: If a corpse «was found close to the border» of the country «or» close «to a city in which the majority» of its inhabitants «are gentiles,» the judges would not break the heifer’s neck, «as it is written: “If one be found» slain” (Deuteronomy 21:1). This «excludes» places where murdered bodies «are» commonly «found,» such as the aforementioned locations."
  }
